// A user `enum OpenMode` beside std.file's private one (DF-153b, closed by
// design 204).
//
// DF-140h gave a module-private `static` inside a std file a module-local
// identity, so a user program may declare its own `ASCII_ZERO` and std still
// reads its own. A module-private TYPE did not get that identity until design
// 204: std.file declares a private `enum OpenMode` (design 155), so a program
// declaring its own used to lose to std's — the user's cases were not there,
// and the error named a declaration the author cannot see, import or find:
//
//     error: enum `OpenMode` has no variant `Write`
//
// A struct or enum name is the shape a user is most likely to pick, and std's
// private types are invisible, so the reserved set was unknowable. Design 82
// makes each std FILE its own module and design 144 makes type identity
// `(defining module, name)`; design 204 is that rule reaching std types.
//
// EXPECT: success
// EXPECT-OUTPUT: 1

enum OpenMode: UInt8 {
    case Read = 0,
    case Write = 1
}

func main() {
    print("{OpenMode.Write as UInt8}")
}
